---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="About | Credits That Count"
  description="Credits That Count is built by Credit Transfer Pros: former and current higher education administrators who have spent years evaluating transfer credit and building degree plans."
>
  <div class="container">
    <section class="block" style="margin-top:26px;">
      <h1>About Credits That Count</h1>
      <p>
        Credits That Count answers one question for students and their
        families: will this credit count? We check courses against the
        public catalogs and transfer sources Louisiana colleges publish,
        and we turn the answer into guidance a family can act on.
      </p>
      <p>
        Our Credit Transfer Pros are former and current higher education
        administrators with experience in college student affairs,
        admissions, and student success.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
      <h2>Who builds and reviews the answers</h2>
      <p>
        The checker and the data behind it are built and reviewed by Credit
        Transfer Pros. Between them, our Pros have spent years evaluating
        transfer credit, reading degree audits, and building degree plans
        inside colleges, in admissions and enrollment services, student
        affairs, and student success offices. They have sat on the side of
        the desk that decides how a credit applies, and they hold every
        answer to the standard they would want for their own family: dated,
        edition stamped, and tied to the published source.
      </p>
      <p>
        When a family or counselor writes in about a result, a Credit
        Transfer Pro reviews the published sources behind the answer before
        we reply, and the data is corrected when a source backs the
        correction.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
      <h2>Where we work</h2>
      <p>
        Louisiana is the first state we serve. Our checker is built on the
        AY 2025-26 statewide common course catalog and the transfer
        information Louisiana colleges make public. We add a state only
        when its public data can support the same standard: verified
        sources, no guessed answers.
      </p>
      <p>
        Only the receiving college makes the final decision on how a
        credit applies. Our work is to make sure a family walks into that
        decision knowing what the published record says.
      </p>
    </section>

    <p class="tagline-foot">Know before you go.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
